    category: "News",
    title: "Published on IEEE Xplore: how small education institutes manage their teachers",
    date: "July 24, 2026",
    excerpt: "We are pleased to announce that the final member of our student group has officially published their research paper in the 2025 IEEE TEMSCON-ASPAC! This marks a fantastic achievement, as we have now seen three separate research papers from this group reach publication. This final study, titled \"HRM Practices in Small-sized Institutes within the Education Industry,\" 👏 Huge congratulations to all the Authors for all their hard work! Check out the full paper here: https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11512168",
    badge: "RUPP",
    author: "Department of Automation & Supply Chain Systems Engineering",
    readTime: "3 min read",
    tags: ["NEWS","News","Department of Automation & Supply Chain Systems Engineering"],
    body: [
      { heading: "Overview", paragraphs: ["Ruppers Abroad · Student Research Published on IEEE Xplore: how small education institutes manage their teachers We are proud to share that the research paper of our student Lonh Piseth has been officially published in the 2025 IEEE TEMSCON-ASPAC proceedings on 13 May 2026. The study, “HRM Practices in Small-sized Institutes within the Education Industry: Evidence from Qualitative Case Studies,” is now available worldwide on IEEE Xplore — and it is the third and final paper from this student group to reach publication. 13 May 2026 Research Publication IEEE TEMSCON-ASPAC 2025 · Bangkok Congratulations Three papers, one student group, all published Lonh Piseth, a student of the Department of Automation & Supply Chain Systems Engineering, presented this work at the 4th IEEE Technology and Engineering Management Society Conference: Asia-Pacific (TEMSCON-ASPAC 2025), held from 14 to 16 September 2025 in Bangkok, Thailand. The paper was presented as Paper 136 in Session 10, Track 4 — Entrepreneurship, Business Models and SocioEconomic Impacts, and the full text has since been indexed on IEEE Xplore. With this publication, all three research papers produced by this student group have now reached publication — a milestone for the department as much as for the authors. Huge congratulations to Lonh Piseth and to every co-author — Sim Duongchan Boremey, Chheng Sovannarith, Seng Vannak and Tieng Kimseng — for all their hard work. Paper HRM Practices in Small-sized Institutes within the Education Industry: Evidence from Qualitative Case Studies Published by IEEE · 2025 IEEE TEMSCON-ASPAC · 13 May 2026 Read it on IEEE Xplore → Lonh Piseth presenting at TEMSCON-ASPAC 2025, 14–16 September 2025, Bangkok, Thailand. Paper 136 in the conference programme — Session 10, Track 4, Phra Erawan Room, 14 September 2025, 13:30–14:30. About the Study How small institutes hire, train and keep their teachers Human Resource Management shapes how any organisation develops, yet small educational institutions rarely have a formal HRM function. In December 2024 the study interviewed the top management of three private educational institutes — STEAM Tuition Centre, Chhouk Meas Centre and Millennium School — at their own offices, in sessions of 90 to 180 minutes, then compared the practices each institute actually uses. 01 Recruitment & selection All three institutes lean on teacher-to-teacher referral as their primary way of finding new teaching staff, rather than on open advertising. 02 Training & development On-the-job training is the key practice, used to build staff capability in classroom management and in teaching methods. 03 Retention & compensation Staff appreciation is organised around a year-end party, seniority payments and benefits awarded on KPI performance. Key takeaway Small institutes should (1) recognise the common framework of Recruitment & Selection, Training & Development and Retention & Compensation; (2) adopt at least teacher-to-teacher referral for hiring, on-the-job training for development, and a year-end party with KPI-based bonus sharing for retention; and (3) design more innovative HRM practices, so that candidates can be drawn from a wider and more competitive pool. Research Team Authors Lonh Piseth Lead author · Royal University of Phnom Penh Sim Duongchan Boremey Co-author · Royal University of Phnom Penh Chheng Sovannarith Co-author · Royal University of Phnom Penh Seng Vannak Co-author · Royal University of Phnom Penh Tieng Kimseng Co-author · Royal University of Phnom Penh The article as it appears on IEEE Xplore. At a Glance Key details Item Detail Title HRM Practices in Small-sized Institutes within the Education Industry: Evidence from Qualitative Case Studies Lead author Lonh Piseth, Royal University of Phnom Penh Co-authors Sim Duongchan Boremey, Chheng Sovannarith, Seng Vannak, Tieng Kimseng Conference 2025 IEEE TEMSCON-ASPAC — 4th IEEE Technology and Engineering Management Society Conference: Asia-Pacific Dates & venue 14–16 September 2025, Bangkok, Thailand Session Session 10 · Track 4: Entrepreneurship, Business Models and SocioEconomic Impacts · Paper 136, Phra Erawan Room, 14 September 2025, 13:30–14:30 Publisher IEEE Published on IEEE Xplore 13 May 2026 Article link ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11512168 Acknowledgement “Three papers from one group of students, all of them now on IEEE Xplore — that is what happens when curiosity is given the time and the support it needs.” Automation & Supply Chain Systems Engineering Faculty of Engineering · Royal University of Phnom Penh"] },
    ]
