    category: "Exchange Program",
    title: "MOU Signing Between RUPP & Adelaide Education Group, Australia",
    date: "July 14, 2026",
    excerpt: "RUPP and Adelaide Education Group Sign MOU for Academic Collaboration On March 31, 2026, the Royal University of Phnom Penh (RUPP) solidified a strategic partnership with the Adelaide Education Group (AEG), Australia, to establish new academic and international avenues. The agreement introduces dual degree programs—offering 2+2 options for undergraduate students and 3+2 pathways for postgraduate students through the Adelaide Institute of Higher Education. In addition to these degree tracks, the collaboration paves the way for student and faculty exchanges, long-distance methodology sharing, and collaborative research projects designed to enrich the educational experiences of both institutions.",
    badge: "RUPP",
    author: "Department of Automation & Supply Chain Systems Engineering",
    readTime: "2 min read",
    tags: ["NEWS","Exchange Program","Department of Automation & Supply Chain Systems Engineering","MOU","Exchange"],
    body: [
      { heading: "Overview", paragraphs: ["Memorandum of Understanding MOU Signing Between RUPP & Adelaide Education Group, Australia The Royal University of Phnom Penh partners with the Adelaide Education Group to open dual degree pathways, exchange teaching staff and students, and build joint academic projects between Cambodia and Australia. Signed 31 March 2026 Academic Collaboration Written by Tieng Kimseng Representatives of the Royal University of Phnom Penh and the Adelaide Education Group, Australia, following the signing ceremony. Overview A partnership for the next generation On 31 March 2026, the Royal University of Phnom Penh (RUPP) signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) with the Adelaide Education Group (AEG), Australia. In the MOU, both parties intend to work within the scope set out below. Scope of Cooperation What the MOU covers 01 Dual degree programs Establish a dual degree program — for example, 2+2 for the Bachelor’s degree program and 3+2 for the Master’s degree program — between the Adelaide Institute of Higher Education and the Royal University of Phnom Penh. 02 Exchange of personnel Exchange of personnel, including teaching staff and students, and other related programs, based on mutual agreement. 03 Study abroad opportunities Offer opportunities to study abroad at the Adelaide Institute of Higher Education. 04 Joint projects & symposia Conducting joint projects that are of mutual benefit to both parties. This may include the organization of a symposium to facilitate the sharing of teaching methodologies and learning experiences in both countries. 05 Long-distance exchange Long-distance exchange of teaching and learning methodologies and experiences between teachers from both countries by means of the internet, video conferencing, or other relevant technologies. 06 Other forms of cooperation Other forms of cooperation, as mutually agreed, may arise as the program develops. RUPP “We work and create opportunities for the next generation.” The Ceremony MOU Signing The MOU was signed between His Excellency Prof. Dr. Chet Chealy (right-hand side), Rector of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, and Mr. Don Chen (left-hand side), President of the Adelaide Education Group (AEG), Australia. Signing of the Memorandum of Understanding at the Royal University of Phnom Penh. Both parties present the signed Memorandum of Understanding. At a Glance Key details Item Detail Date signed 31 March 2026 Parties Royal University of Phnom Penh (RUPP) & Adelaide Education Group (AEG), Australia Signatories His Excellency Prof. Dr. Chet Chealy, Rector, RUPP · Mr. Don Chen, President, Adelaide Education Group, Australia Dual degree pathways 2+2 for the Bachelor’s degree program and 3+2 for the Master’s degree program, with the Adelaide Institute of Higher Education Benefits Exchange of teaching staff and students, study abroad opportunities, joint projects and symposia, long-distance exchange of teaching methodologies Automation & Supply Chain Systems Engineering Faculty of Engineering · Royal University of Phnom Penh Written by Tieng Kimseng"] },
    ]
